                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A. The Union and the University hereby agree to meet every other month at each medical center location to address staffing issues and to try to develop reasonable workload guidelines. The parties may agree to meet more or less often.\nCampus location means all work units associated with a campus, including those at off-campus sites. Such meetings will occur in accordance with the following:",
            "block_bbox": [
                109,
                595,
                1119,
                736
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    109.0,
                    595.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    595.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    736.0
                ],
                [
                    109.0,
                    736.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. The Union must request a meeting and the parties must agree to the meeting date.",
            "block_bbox": [
                183,
                760,
                1119,
                815
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    183.0,
                    760.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    760.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    815.0
                ],
                [
                    183.0,
                    815.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. The Union must submit a written agenda identifying staffing concerns it wishes to discuss. Such agenda must be submitted to the designated campus representative at least ten (10) work days before the proposed meeting date.",
            "block_bbox": [
                181,
                842,
                1120,
                929
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    181.0,
                    842.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    842.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    929.0
                ],
                [
                    181.0,
                    929.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. In the event the University has agenda items regarding staffing, the University shall present its agenda to the Union at least ten (10) work days before the scheduled meeting.",
            "block_bbox": [
                181,
                953,
                1120,
                1039
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    181.0,
                    953.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    953.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    1039.0
                ],
                [
                    181.0,
                    1039.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. In the event neither party submits an agenda item ten (10) work days before the scheduled meeting, the meeting will not be convened.",
            "block_bbox": [
                182,
                1064,
                1119,
                1122
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    182.0,
                    1064.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    1064.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    1122.0
                ],
                [
                    182.0,
                    1122.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "5. Individuals who can effectively address the staffing issues that are identified in the submitted agenda will represent each party at the meeting",
            "block_bbox": [
                183,
                1146,
                1120,
                1204
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    183.0,
                    1146.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    1146.0
                ],
                [
                    1120.0,
                    1204.0
                ],
                [
                    183.0,
                    1204.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "6. The staffing committee will be made up of no more than four (4) Union representatives and four (4) management representatives. Additional individuals may attend by written agreement of the parties. The Union must submit a written request for employee release time at least seven (7) work days before the scheduled meeting. Such employees will be counted as union representatives, and the release time shall be granted unless operational requirements determine otherwise. Permission to attend these meetings shall not be unreasonably denied.",
            "block_bbox": [
                179,
                1229,
                1121,
                1454
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    179.0,
                    1229.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    1229.0
                ],
                [
                    1121.0,
                    1454.0
                ],
                [
                    179.0,
                    1454.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "7. The Union may present staffing concerns and propose solutions at the staffing committee meetings.",
            "block_bbox": [
                182,
                1477,
                1119,
                1535
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 12,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    182.0,
                    1477.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    1477.0
                ],
                [
                    1119.0,
                    1535.0
                ],
                [
                    182.0,
                    1535.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "8. The parties may use the meetings to discuss the issues pertaining to custodial workload, with the square footage conversion table referenced in the Side Letter of September 26, 2001, as one consideration in the discussions. The University recognizes that custodial work may be performed by individuals in classifications other than “custodian” at some campuses/hospitals/laboratories.",
